VALUES ('Sonic The Hedgehog', 'By 1990, the Japanese video game company Sega wanted a foothold in the video game console market with its 16-bit console, the Sega Genesis. Sega''s efforts had been stymied by the dominance of Nintendo; the Genesis did not have a large install base and Nintendo did not take Sega seriously as a competitor. Sega of America CEO Michael Katz attempted to challenge Nintendo with the "Genesis ', TO_VECTOR(TO_CLOB('[0.05356608, 0.03938324, 0.08131786, -0.11788531, -0.01145931, 0.01886634, -0.01650972, 0.07385740, -0.02677330, 0.04952621, -0.07573183, 0.06177908, -0.03784929, 0.00447009, 0.02123470, -0.03376438, 0.00169748, -0.01747585, 0.00216601, -0.05287093, 0.02598837, -0.05783344, -0.02605987, -0.05422936, -0.00474727, 0.03212250, 0.00638234, -0.01050255, 0.05988795, -0.04522677, -0.03447307, 0.00866124, 0.08016328, 0.02558607, -0.05604977, -0.05735495, 0.03738726, -0.07432342, -0.09030111, -0.02181088, -0.03173840, 0.10326779, -0.02188755, 0.00011795, 0.02095205, 0.00009599, -0.03565015, -0.04786927, 0.01456596, -0.01138920, -0.03492179, -0.04343375, 0.12804574, -0.03627031, 0.05134595, 0.02649927, -0.00435589, 0.01037992, 0.12685649, 0.05586576, -0.01039513, -0.09588086, 0.02299166, -0.01972118, 0.08587909, -0.03598407, 0.06941406, 0.01946575, -0.10523293, -0.03157150, 0.02993022, -0.02727168, -0.02699006, 0.01742469, -0.04371672, 0.04921186, 0.01321586, 0.04063746, 0.01997889, 0.01111881, -0.01174143, -0.02006735, -0.06825158, 0.00629260, -0.01019892, 0.07078473, 0.00849625, -0.01378520, 0.01986506, 0.12023696, -0.08475649, -0.03244105, 0.13761939, 0.01165739, -0.00285801, -0.03322916, 0.00128171, -0.07991605, 0.04826770, -0.02927328, 0.03321909, 0.06721745, 0.04220448, 0.00198859, 0.03474448, -0.00850260, 0.02497401, -0.01905267, 0.03144048, 0.08434068, -0.01822240, -0.02096096, -0.02275220, 0.03875571, -0.00078786, -0.07000302, -0.03496940, 0.04214927, 0.00433308, 0.00263928, 0.03388564, -0.01322506, -0.05120834, 0.04428425, -0.09416